WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.723
This tutorial uses the Animator to make a figure wave.

2
00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:16.299
You will rig the ready made stick figure, pose one arm, set keyframes with easing, and then apply the motion to your timeline as ordinary keyframes.

3
00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.410
It takes about ten minutes.

4
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:23.480
Open the More menu at the top right and choose Animator.

5
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.174
The Animator opens over the Studio.

6
00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:33.640
Select Stick figure, and ten shapes are placed on the timeline, already rigged and ready to pose.

7
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:38.572
The rig list on the left shows every part of the figure.

8
00:00:38.572 --> 00:00:42.531
A part can hang from a parent and turn about a joint.

9
00:00:42.531 --> 00:00:50.449
Here, the forearm is parented to the upper arm, so rotating the upper arm carries the whole chain with it.

10
00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.660
Select the forearm to inspect its settings.

11
00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.690
Start at zero seconds, which is the rest pose.

12
00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:04.465
Move the playhead to zero point three seconds, and set the forearm's Turn value to minus sixty.

13
00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:07.175
A keyframe is written at the playhead.

14
00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:12.880
Then move to one second, and set Turn to forty, so the arm swings the other way.

15
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.947
Two keys make a wave, but a stiff one.

16
00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:24.628
Select the second key and set its easing to Ease, so the arm starts and finishes gently.

17
00:01:24.628 --> 00:01:39.380
Then add another pair of keys, at one point seven seconds with a Turn of minus fifty, and at two point four seconds with a Turn of zero, so the arm settles back to rest.

18
00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.183
Press play in the Animator.

19
00:01:42.183 --> 00:01:44.844
The figure waves twice and settles.

20
00:01:44.844 --> 00:01:51.840
You can scrub the playhead to check individual poses, and drag any key diamond to retime it.

21
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.360
Keys snap to frames.

22
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.184
When the motion is right, press Apply to edit.

23
00:01:57.184 --> 00:02:02.599
The Animator closes and the motion is baked onto the clips as ordinary keyframes.

24
00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:10.820
Open the Animate workspace and select the forearm to see its rotation curve, which you can adjust like any other keyframes.

25
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.528
That completes the Animator tutorial.

26
00:02:14.528 --> 00:02:21.884
Because the result is plain keyframes, the preview, the FFmpeg export and the API all agree.

27
00:02:21.884 --> 00:02:29.080
The next tutorial covers block coding, which builds repeatable edits without writing code.

